1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,655
Imagine government services where AI agents don't just respond.

2
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:08,690
They act, collaborate, and complete tasks for citizens.

3
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:15,714
But even a trusted agent can attempt an action it was never authorized to perform.

4
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:24,064
WAKALA verifies who the agent is, what authority it was given,

5
00:00:24,064 --> 00:00:27,042
and whether this specific action is permitted.

6
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:32,141
If it exceeds that authority, WAKALA stops it, before execution.

7
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,311
And this isn't just a concept.

8
00:00:34,661 --> 00:00:39,270
Our working prototype enforces that decision through a real authorization gateway.

9
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:43,704
An authorized officer can contain the incident,

10
00:00:43,704 --> 00:00:47,858
restore valid authority, and let the legitimate service continue.

11
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:53,333
Security, without unnecessary disruption.

12
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:59,912
WAKALA. Autonomous AI. Accountable actions.
